It is getting late.
I want to go home.
This time I ask nobody for directions.
I find an information board with a city map.
I look at the map.
The way to the station is not far.
I think of the man's words: Go straight ahead.
I do that.
I walk straight ahead and look for a sign.
There it is.
The sign is green with a white S.
I continue walking straight ahead.
The path is right by the water.
Here is a small park.
I walk past the park.
The next sign points to the right.
I turn right.
Over there is the S-Bahn station.
I walk to the station.
Soon I will be in my flat.
